{# Decision template: will a rumour be remembered, once it has run its course? (ADR-001, "Lifecycle")
   One request per candidate, sent by Promote.cpp when a rumour retires stale having reached a fair
   share of people (promote.min_reach). The DLL reads `lasting`, a noul whose probability of true
   must reach promote.lasting (0.4) for the rumour to become world knowledge.

   Asked of the first telling, not of how juicy any version made it. Calibrated on the user's save
   (141 rumours, 2026-11-20) with tools/lasting_panel.py:
     Jev 1.14   the declaration of war 0.78; made-up yardsticks: Alduin's return 0.81, a dragon
                slain at Whiterun 0.69, Ulfric killed 0.64, the Harbinger killed 0.47, a Jarl
                murdered 0.44; the war's skirmishes, proclamations and guild errands 0.35 or less;
                harvested flings, fights and sales 0.04 to 0.18.
     d3:4b      reads higher and orders less cleanly: war 0.88, Jarl 0.85, dragon 0.74, but the
                Hjaalmarch necromancers 0.73 and skirmishes up to 0.65. About 0.75 there.
     Kev-4B     (kev:4b-q8_0) reads higher and takes proclamations and letters between factions
                for big news: war 0.84, Alduin 0.76, dragon 0.6 to 0.7 by the wording, a faction
                letter 0.67, proclamations up to 0.64, Ulfric killed 0.58, the Harbinger 0.52, a
                Jarl 0.49, the Maven warrant 0.33, harvested 0.47 at most. About 0.6 there: 5 of
                the save's 145 kept, the war and 4 proclamations or letters.

   Context: lasting_text. A criterion is exactly one line. #}
[ state setting ]
{{ render_template("submodules\\system_head\\0010_setting") }}
[ end state ]

[ state rumour ]
{{ lasting_text }}
[ end state ]

[ question lasting noul ]
`rumour` went round Skyrim by word of mouth. A year from now, will ordinary people across Skyrim still remember it and bring it up, the way people remember a war breaking out, a Jarl killed or a dragon slain? Judge the matter itself, not how juicy the telling is.
[ criteria ]
true: Yes: it will be remembered and talked of across Skyrim for a year or more.
false: No: within a season it will be old talk, remembered only by those it touched.
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
